<title>USA: US exporters report 112,000 tonnes wheat to Israel.</title>
<headline>US exporters report 112,000 tonnes wheat to Israel.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department Thursday said private exporters reported sales of 112,000 tonnes of wheat to Israel for delivery during the 1997/98 marketing year.</p>
<p>USDA said the sale included 100,000 tonnes of hard red winter wheat and 12,000 tonnes of soft red winter wheat.</p>
<p>The marketing year for wheat began June 1.</p>
<p>USDA issues both daily and weekly export sales reports.</p>
<p>Exporters must report to USDA sales of 100,000 tonnes or more of one commodity made in one day to a single destination by 1500 ET the next business day after the sale.</p>
<p>Sales of lesser quantities must be reported weekly.</p>
</text>
